SUMMARY:Deadline: Harry Ransom Center Research Fellowships 2027-2028 (Austi
 n\, Texas)
DESCRIPTION:The Harry Ransom Center at The University of Texas at Austin aw
 ards research fellowships for on-site work in its collections spanning lit
 erature\, photography\, film\, art\, performing arts\, music and cultural 
 history\, supporting scholarly articles\, dissertations\, creative works\,
  digital humanities projects and exhibition proposals. FELLOWSHIP TYPES: P
 ostdoctoral Fellowships of USD 3\,500 per month for one or two months\, op
 en to holders of a PhD or terminal degree (MFA\, MLIS)\, current or former
  faculty\, and similarly qualified researchers without institutional affil
 iation\; Dissertation Fellowships of USD 2\,500 for graduate students with
  doctoral dissertations in progress\; and Travel Stipends of USD 2\,000 op
 en to graduate students\, current or former faculty and independent resear
 chers including journalists and artists (not combinable with other Ransom 
 Center fellowships). International recipients in all categories receive an
  additional one-time USD 500 stipend toward visa and travel costs. Fellows
  spend most days in the Reading Room consulting the collections\, with acc
 ess to a shared office\, during a residency period between 1 June 2027 and
  31 August 2028. APPLY with a three-page proposal PDF and letters of recom
 mendation\; recommendation letters are also due by the deadline. DEADLINE:
  6 November 2026\, 5:00 PM CST.\n\nOrganisation: Harry Ransom Center\, The
  University of Texas at Austin\nLocation: Austin\, Texas\, USA. On-site re
 search in the Ransom Center's collections\; international applicants welco
 me and receive an additional one-time USD 500 stipend for visa and travel 
 costs.\nAward: Postdoctoral Fellowships: USD 3\,500 per month for one or t
 wo months. Dissertation Fellowships: USD 2\,500. Travel Stipends: USD 2\,0
 00 (open to graduate students\, faculty and independent researchers includ
 ing artists and journalists). International recipients get an extra USD 50
 0. No application fee.\nDuration: One to two months on-site\, taken betwee
 n 1 June 2027 and 31 August 2028.\n\nMore: https://www.hrc.utexas.edu/fell
 owships/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.hrc.utexas.edu/fellowships/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Austin\, Texas\, USA. On-site research in the Ransom Center's coll
 ections\; international applicants welcome and receive an additional one-t
 ime USD 500 stipend for visa and travel costs.
