DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261204
SUMMARY:Deadline: J. Anthony Lukas Work-in-Progress Awards 2027
DESCRIPTION:The J. Anthony Lukas Work-in-Progress Awards\, given jointly by
  Columbia Journalism School and the Nieman Foundation at Harvard\, are ope
 n for 2027 submissions. Two annual awards of USD 25\,000 each help writers
  complete a book-length work of narrative nonfiction on a topic of America
 n political or social concern\; books on science\, technology and media ac
 countability have won in past years. Applicants need a fully executed cont
 ract with a US-based publisher for the book in progress. There is no entry
  fee for the Work-in-Progress awards\; note that the Lukas Book Prize and 
 the Mark Lynton History Prize run on the same portal with the same deadlin
 e but carry a USD 75 entry fee. TO APPLY: submit via the Columbia Journali
 sm Awards Submittable portal. DEADLINE: 3 December 2026\, 11:59 PM ET.\n\n
 Organisation: Columbia Journalism School and the Nieman Foundation\nLocati
 on: USA. Requires a fully executed contract with a US-based publisher.\nAw
 ard: Two awards of USD 25\,000 each. No entry fee for the Work-in-Progress
  awards.\n\nMore: https://columbiajournalismawards.submittable.com/submit?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://columbiajournalismawards.submittable.com/submit?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:USA. Requires a fully executed contract with a US-based publisher.
